Configuration Management Plan (CMP) Template

1. Introduction

1.1 Purpose
Describe the purpose of this document and its importance for the project.

1.2 Scope
Detail the project name, its objectives, and what the CMP covers (e.g., tools, processes, roles).

1.3 Definitions and Acronyms
Provide definitions of terms and acronyms used in the document.

2. Roles and Responsibilities

Define the roles and responsibilities of all personnel involved in configuration management:
	•	Configuration Manager:
	•	Project Manager:
	•	Developers/QA:
	•	Release Manager:

3. Configuration Identification

3.1 Items to be Managed
List the artifacts that will be tracked (e.g., source code, documentation, test cases, build scripts).

3.2 Naming Conventions
Specify naming conventions for artifacts (e.g., feature_branch_[ticket_number]).

3.3 Versioning Scheme
Detail the versioning policy (e.g., semantic versioning, YYYY.MM.DD).

4. Configuration Control

4.1 Change Control Process
Outline the process for requesting, approving, and implementing changes.

4.2 Change Control Board (CCB)
List members of the CCB and their responsibilities.

4.3 Tools Used
Specify tools for change tracking (e.g., JIRA, Git, Jenkins).

5. Configuration Status Accounting

Describe how the status of configuration items will be recorded and tracked (e.g., automated reports, manual logs).

6. Audits and Reviews

6.1 Configuration Audits
Explain the process for ensuring compliance with CM standards (e.g., periodic audits).

6.2 Baseline Reviews
Detail reviews to confirm the correctness of baselines.

7. Tools and Environment

7.1 Version Control System
Specify tools (e.g., Git, SVN).

7.2 Build Tools
List tools for building and deployment (e.g., Jenkins, Maven).

7.3 Issue Tracking Tools
Mention tools for tracking issues (e.g., JIRA, Bugzilla).

8. Backup and Recovery

8.1 Backup Strategy
Define frequency and method of backups for critical items.

8.2 Recovery Plan
Explain steps for recovery in case of data loss or corruption.

9. Maintenance and Updates

Detail how the CMP will be maintained and updated throughout the project lifecycle.

10. Approval and Sign-Off

Include a table for approvals:

Role	Name	Date	Signature
Project Manager	[Name]	[Date]	[Signature]
Configuration Manager	[Name]	[Date]	[Signature]

